      "writtenOn": "2025-09-29T11:50:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hmm... we shouldn\u0027t do this before donating?\n\nThe AI here suggests to donate the first page first just to read the size, we could do that, but it would be much easier to leverage aosp/3666638?\n\n...But actually, do we need to pass this size to the hypervisor at all? It is still the global constant `pkvm_vcpu_sz`, the hypervisor still knows this constant, nothing changed, right?",
      "fixSuggestions": [
        {
          "fixId": "90a434bf_b29a6e67",
          "description": "prompt_to_edit API",
          "replacements": [
            {
              "path": "arch/x86/kvm/pkvm/pkvm.c",
              "range": {
                "startLine": 305,
                "startChar": 0,
                "endLine": 305,
                "endChar": 0
              },
              "replacement": "\n\t// Donate the first page to securely read the size.\n\tret \u003d donate_host_memory(va, PAGE_SIZE);\n\tif (ret)\n\t\treturn ret;\n\n"
            },
            {
              "path": "arch/x86/kvm/pkvm/pkvm.c",
              "range": {
                "startLine": 307,
                "startChar": 0,
                "endLine": 308,
                "endChar": 0
              },
              "replacement": "\t\tgoto undonate_first_page;\n"
            },
