      "writtenOn": "2025-09-30T05:40:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Hmm... we shouldn\u0027t do this before donating?\n\nNot sure if there is any potential issue if we read size from the memory page before donating it?\n\n\u003e ...But actually, do we need to pass this size to the hypervisor at all? It is still the global constant pkvm_vcpu_sz, the hypervisor still knows this constant, nothing changed, right?\n\nIndeed. The sizes of pkvm_vcpu is constant to pkvm for creating. The reason to store size is to have a way for the host to know if it doesn\u0027t allocate enough memory pages, e.g., the size is extended by pkvm but forget to extend at host side, then we will know that easily. Probably this is not important as we can find out this by other way. I can try not to store the size in the passed in memory pages.\n\n\u003e but it would be much easier to leverage aosp/3666638?\n\nIf we want to pass in the sizes as well, then probably we will need 5 inputs for this PV interface (shared_vcpu, pkvm_vcpu_gpa, pkvm_vcpu_size, fpu_gpa, fpu_size). But as we would like to try to limit the inputs as 4 in v6.15, so probably we can try to use constant size to avoid increasing the inputs first.",
      "parentUuid": "6b5a31f9_c4df0ddf",
      "revId": "714118bd87e0ae391c94826a741feeacf729ef8a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "56bf0af5_b417e02b",
        "filename": "arch/x86/kvm/pkvm/pkvm.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 305,
      "author": {
        "id": 2022314
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-09-30T11:02:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Not sure if there is any potential issue if we read size from the memory page before donating it?\n\nIt is probably not as bad as writing to it, but still, it may be not even mapped in the hypervisor\u0027s page tables (thus causing a page fault in pKVM), or for example it may be a MMIO address, so reading it may have who knows what side effects?\n\nSo it seems safer to prevent that, by properly going through the page state API to at least validate this address?",
      "parentUuid": "6ea102f8_371e90cc",
      "revId": "714118bd87e0ae391c94826a741feeacf729ef8a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8289f55b_529f51f1",
        "filename": "arch/x86/kvm/pkvm/pkvm.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 305,
      "author": {
        "id": 4085392
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-09-30T14:26:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e It is probably not as bad as writing to it, but still, it may be not even mapped in the hypervisor\u0027s page tables (thus causing a page fault in pKVM), or for example it may be a MMIO address, so reading it may have who knows what side effects?\n\nMMIO is also not mapped in the pkvm thus should also a page fault.\n\nAnyway, I will change this with constant size thus no need to read from the memory before donating.",
      "parentUuid": "56bf0af5_b417e02b",
      "revId": "714118bd87e0ae391c94826a741feeacf729ef8a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
